      "writtenOn": "2022-12-12T19:38:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two values per cpu in Sudhin\u0027s share memory mechanism. My understanding is that one of them is a request from Trusty and the other is for Linux to inform Trusty of the actual priority. Is this correct?\n\nThe intention of this new trusty_set_actual_nice() is to inform Trusty of actual. I think I see what you are getting at with this comment ... should this call to inform trusty be done before every SMC call? Or only every NOP call?",
      "parentUuid": "7d9402f8_473452ea",
      "revId": "3a79521211517287099219564f88559e5a9eb1bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
